  "limitations": [
    "Data appear SYNTHETIC (suspected): uniform features, no tool/time/unit ID, 20 negative VB_mm values; Wear_Class is a deterministic binning of VB_mm.",
    "Pseudo-time is the rank of VB_mm, so VB is monotone in pseudo-time by construction. The time index is target-derived; it is the SAME input for physics, data-driven and hybrid models (round-1 mismatch fixed), but none of the three is an independent predictive test. The physics row is a trend fit.",
    "Features explain almost nothing: max|Pearson r|=0.059, RF CV R2 random=-0.022, blocked=-0.120 (features only, no time input).",
    "Held-out evaluation uses 400 rows in 4 contiguous blocks. The paired bootstrap resamples rows i.i.d., which is optimistic for sorted, autocorrelated rows; the intervals are not a block-bootstrap result.",
    "RUL is in pseudo-time units (PTU, 1 PTU = one sorted sample index), not hours or cycles.",
    "RUL truth (first sorted index with VB >= 0.30 minus stage time) is CIRCULAR by construction: it is derived from the same target the models are fitted to. 'truth in 95%' entries are not validation. Conclusions concern the method, not a real machine tool.",
    "c_w is sign-constrained to [0, 430] (force range / VB range on training rows). Its posterior sd is 58.2 against a prior sd of 124; the 75% ratio 0.469 is reported with the absolute sd and should be read as weak identification, not information gain.",
    "MCMC: 32 walkers, 1000 burn-in, 5000 steps per stage. Minimum steps/tau = 10.9 (target >= 50): NOT met; chains are flagged as unconverged in the metrics.",
    "Surrogate horizon 6000 PTU is 3x the 2000-row record; the forcing is wrapped periodically beyond 2000 PTU, so RUL beyond 2000 PTU rests on that assumption. RUL censored at horizon in 3.8 % of Sobol samples and 6.2 % of 50%-life posterior draws.",
    "Surrogate trained on fixed-step RK4 (dt=1 PTU). Against the reference RK45 ODE the max |difference| on 30 designs is 0.0236 mm (0.079 x VB_crit). Speed-up is reported against RK45.",
    "Coverage: nominal 95% held-out coverage is 1.000 with mean width 1.387 mm against held-out residual sd of 0.0036 mm for the physics trend fit. The band is dominated by GP variance (median held-out GP sd 0.3364 mm, about 123 times the median posterior sigma_obs of 0.0027 mm). The GP sd is inflated by the 6000-PTU horizon: the surrogate RMSE over the full grid is 1.012 mm.",
    "Hybrid minus physics held-out RMSE = -0.00162 mm, bootstrap 95% CI [-0.002266470611180295, -0.0011484014546302784] (i.i.d. rows). Data-driven (RF+t) minus physics = +0.00511 mm, CI [0.0042951553898922966, 0.005908712699747151].",
    "Costs c_p=1, c_f=5 and derating law (gamma=0.5, d_min=0.7) are assumptions. At 50% life the raw derating value 0.755 is not clamped.",
    "Calibration uses one pseudo-trajectory (no unit replicates); the posterior is conditional on the GP surrogate and on the assumed noise and force model.",
    "Posterior RUL uses GP mean trajectories; GP variance and sigma_obs enter the likelihood and the coverage band, not the RUL draws.",
    "Nominal constants (sigma_n, Ea/R, C_th, T_inf, eta, T rise) are fixed, not fitted; only k1, k2, alpha, hA are fitted in the trend fit and calibrated, and vc is fixed at 1 in calibration.",
    "F_res = sqrt(CF_1^2+CF_2^2+CF_3^2) is a combination of feature columns, not measured Fx,Fy,Fz.",
    "Vibration/AE are single snapshot values per row; no windowed RMS/std."
  ],
